 the solid that separates is generally","options":["pure solid solvent","pure solid solute","a 1:1 compound always","ice that contains all the solute"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"The solute stays in the liquid; the first solid is almost always the pure solvent.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"easy","concept_id":"freezing-depression","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-230","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"A larger $K_f$ at the same molality produces","options":["a larger depression","a smaller depression","no change","an elevation instead"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"$\\Delta T_f$ scales with $K_f$ when m is fixed.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"easy","concept_id":"freezing-depression","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-231","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"Common salt is scattered on icy roads because NaCl","options":["lowers the melting point of ice","raises the boiling point of ice","oxidises ice","absorbs all sunlight"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"Dissolved ions depress the freezing point, so ice melts at the ambient winter temperature.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"easy","concept_id":"freezing-depression","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-232","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"The unit of $K_f$ is","options":["K kg mol⁻¹","L atm mol⁻¹","mol L⁻¹","joule only"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"The same d